From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 00:49:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02221/11362] [outer-loop] E1: salience-ordered candidates +
 deterministic HUD-masking (arXiv:2512.24156)

The two zero-quota ingredients our explorer was missing vs the graph-explore SOTA:
- rich_action_candidates now orders click candidates by VISUAL SALIENCE (segment
  area x color-rarity) so the search tries interactive-looking objects before HUD/
  texture -- finds wins within a smaller budget. Pure ordering; replay still valid.
- discover_hud_mask() deterministically finds STEP-DRIVEN HUD cells (a counter that
  advances identically regardless of action) and graph_explore_solve_v2(mask_hud=True)
  masks them out of node identity -- fixes the state-explosion/aliasing that made
  tu93 reach L2 but fail the reproduction gate. Mask computed ONCE (stationary).

Regression-gated: all 8 banked solves still reproduce (metaharness=10); explorer
re-finds cd82/sp80/su15/tu93 at the same levels under both salience and mask_hud
(HUD cells found: cd82=1, sp80=2, tu93=1, su15=0 -- real counters confirmed).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
